Dithienylethenes are another family of photoresponsive organic groups applied in the preparation of switchable MOFs. Triggered by UC or visible light, dithienylethenes undergo reversible ring opening/closing. Diarylethene derivatives such as dithienylethenes are distinguished in the excellent thermal stability of both the open and closed isomers, limiting the extent of unintended back reaction to the more thermally stable isomer over time. Dithienylethenes display desirable
