Far less studied in MOFs than azobenzenes or dithienylethenes, spiropyrans are an alternative class of photoactive molecule that are capable of reversibly converting between a colorless “closed” spiropyran form (CSP) under the influence of visible light or heat, and a colored “open” merocyanine form (OMC) upon UV light irradiation. Rather than cis/trans isomerization as in the case of azobenzenes, and similar to dithienylethenes, spiropyrans undergo reversible ring opening/closing switching mechanism.
