Pressure and temperature are interesting stimuli partially due to the various occasions in which they arise. In some industrial processes, failure of pressure-relieving mechanisms or unplanned for accumulation of heat can be dangerous. Smart materials with switch-off capabilities may work to prevent further build-up (as in the case of thermal runaway) and minimize damage to surrounding components. Therefore, although these switching cases may be secondary functions, such safety features can easily be envisioned as essential to meet industrial standards or consumer expectations in the near future.
